index c2dd2b6..94b56e2 100644
--- a/docs/options.md
+++ b/docs/options.md
@@ -17,6 +17,18 @@ Useful and often used kwargs are:
 - `required`: Makes option required.
 - `type`: Sets {ref}`parameter type <parameter-types>`
 
+Commands may enable `track_changes` to inspect option assignments with
+`ctx.get_option_history`. The history records final values and their
+parameter sources per context; later direct assignments to `ctx.params`
+use `source=None`.
+
+Look up an option by its parameter name or a declared spelling, such as
+`--count`. Disabled tracking returns `None`; enabled tracking returns an
+empty list for unknown names, arguments, or options without exposed
+values. Each record includes a floating-point timestamp. Queries copy
+the list and record dictionaries, but do not copy the recorded values
+themselves.
+
 ```{contents}
